According to the specification, a UE initiates the FailureInformation procedure "upon detecting failure for an RLC bearer, in accordance with 5.3.10.3". 

Additionally, the UE shall set FailureInfoRLC-Bearer as follows: 
- set logicalChannelIdentity to the logical channel identity of the failing RLC bearer;
- set cellGroupId to the cell group identity of the failing RLC bearer;
- set the failureType as rlc-failure. 

The FailureInformation message is then submitted to lower layers for transmission via SRB1 if the failure is for an MCG RLC bearer, or via SRB3 if the failure is for an SCG RLC bearer.

A UE initiates the FailureInformation procedure when there is a need to inform the network about a failure detected by the UE, specifically:

- Upon detecting failure for an RLC bearer, in accordance with 5.3.10.3;
- Upon detecting DAPS handover failure, in accordance with 5.3.5.8.3.

